        <h1 class="heading-1 mb-6">Grokipedia Editing Policy: How AI Content Generation Differs from Wikipedia</h1>

        <p class="text-xl text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          Understanding <strong>Grokipedia's editing policy</strong> is essential for users comparing AI-generated encyclopedias with traditional human-edited platforms like Wikipedia. This guide explains how Grokipedia creates and manages content, its moderation approach, and why users cannot directly edit articles.
        </p>

        <!-- Policy Overview Box -->
        <div class="mt-8 p-6 bg-purple-50 dark:bg-purple-950/20 border-l-4 border-purple-500 rounded-lg">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-3 text-purple-900 dark:text-purple-100">Grokipedia Editing Policy Overview</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-purple-800 dark:text-purple-200">
            <li>• <strong>No User Editing:</strong> Grokipedia does not allow public users to edit or create articles</li>
            <li>• <strong>AI-Generated Content:</strong> All articles are created by xAI's Grok large language model</li>
            <li>• <strong>Real-Time Updates:</strong> Content is dynamically generated and updated by AI systems</li>
            <li>• <strong>Centralized Control:</strong> xAI maintains full editorial control over all content</li>
            <li>• <strong>No Edit History:</strong> Unlike Wikipedia, there is no public revision history</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
