        <h2>What is Grokipedia's Editing Policy?</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Grokipedia's editing policy</strong> fundamentally differs from traditional encyclopedias like Wikipedia. Instead of allowing community members to collaboratively edit and create articles, Grokipedia relies entirely on artificial intelligence for content generation and management.
        </p>

        <p>
          This approach represents a paradigm shift in how encyclopedic content is created, maintained, and updated. While Wikipedia has built its reputation on the "wisdom of crowds" model with millions of volunteer editors, Grokipedia takes the opposite approach by centralizing all content creation within xAI's Grok AI system.
        </p>

        <h2>Core Principles of Grokipedia Content Policy</h2>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 my-8">
          <div class="p-6 bg-blue-50 dark:bg-blue-950/20 rounded-lg border border-blue-200 dark:border-blue-800">
            <h4 class="font-semibold mb-3 text-blue-800 dark:text-blue-200">AI-First Content Generation</h4>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300">
              <li><strong>Automated Creation:</strong> Articles generated by Grok LLM</li>
              <li><strong>Dynamic Updates:</strong> Content refreshed in real-time</li>
              <li><strong>Consistency:</strong> Uniform writing style across articles</li>
              <li><strong>Speed:</strong> Rapid content generation at scale</li>
              <li><strong>Coverage:</strong> Ability to cover vast range of topics</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="p-6 bg-green-50 dark:bg-green-950/20 rounded-lg border border-green-200 dark:border-green-800">
            <h4 class="font-semibold mb-3 text-green-800 dark:text-green-200">Centralized Editorial Control</h4>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-green-700 dark:text-green-300">
              <li><strong>xAI Oversight:</strong> All content controlled by xAI</li>
              <li><strong>No Vandalism:</strong> Eliminates malicious edits</li>
              <li><strong>Quality Control:</strong> Consistent moderation standards</li>
              <li><strong>Liability:</strong> Clear content responsibility</li>
              <li><strong>Brand Safety:</strong> Controlled content output</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2>Can Users Edit Grokipedia Articles?</h2>
        <div class="bg-yellow-50 dark:bg-yellow-950/20 p-6 rounded-lg my-8 border-l-4 border-yellow-500">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-3 text-yellow-900 dark:text-yellow-100">Short Answer: No</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-yellow-800 dark:text-yellow-200 mb-4">
            <strong>Users cannot directly edit, modify, or create articles on Grokipedia.</strong> This is a fundamental design decision that distinguishes Grokipedia from Wikipedia and other wiki-based platforms.
          </p>
          <div class="space-y-2 text-sm text-yellow-700 dark:text-yellow-300">
            <p><strong>What users CAN do:</strong></p>
            <ul class="ml-4 space-y-1">
              <li>• Read and browse articles</li>
              <li>• Search for information</li>
              <li>• Share articles via links</li>
              <li>• Interact with AI for clarifications (via Grok chat)</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="mt-3"><strong>What users CANNOT do:</strong></p>
            <ul class="ml-4 space-y-1">
              <li>• Edit existing articles</li>
              <li>• Create new articles</li>
              <li>• Add references or citations</li>
              <li>• Participate in editorial discussions</li>
              <li>• View or revert to previous versions</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

